  "worked_solution": "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{\u2015}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{\u2015}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\overset{\u2015}{x}=10,$ $z=2,$ and $\\sigma =1.5$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{\u2015}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ x & =10+2\\cdot 1.5 \\\\ x & =10+3 \\\\ x & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
